#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# bit_shift_right

#% text
# `bit_shift_right(k, s)` shifts the integer `k` right by `s` bits: `floor(k/2^s)`, also for negative `k`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
bit_shift_right(1000, 3)
#% output
#= 125

#% cell
bit_shift_right(-9, 1)
#% output
#= -5

#% cell
bit_shift_right([8, 16, 33], 2)
#% output
#= [2, 4, 8]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `bit_length`, `bit_flip`, `bit_and`
